    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Description</b></p>

<p>As a <b>Support Operations Manager</b>,<br/>
I want newly created cases to be automatically assigned to available agents using a round-robin method,<br/>
So that workload is distributed fairly and cases are handled efficiently without manual intervention.</p>

<p><b>Acceptance Criteria</b></p>

<h3><a name="1%EF%B8%8F%E2%83%A3AutomaticAssignment"></a>1️⃣ Automatic Assignment</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Given a new case is created</li>
	<li>When the case enters the system</li>
	<li>Then the system should automatically assign it to an eligible agent</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="2%EF%B8%8F%E2%83%A3RoundRobinDistribution"></a>2️⃣ Round-Robin Distribution</h3>

<ul>
	<li>The system should assign cases using a <b>round-robin allocation logic</b></li>
	<li>Cases should be distributed evenly among eligible agents</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="3%EF%B8%8F%E2%83%A3AgentAvailabilityCheck"></a>3️⃣ Agent Availability Check</h3>

<p>Before assigning a case, the system must verify:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Agent status is <b>Active</b></li>
	<li>Agent is currently within defined <b>working hours</b></li>
	<li>Agent is not marked as <b>Vacation / Out of Office</b></li>
	<li>Agent is not in <b>Inactive / Disabled</b> status</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="4%EF%B8%8F%E2%83%A3ExclusionCriteria"></a>4️⃣ Exclusion Criteria</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Cases must NOT be assigned to agents who:
	<ul>
		<li>Are on vacation</li>
		<li>Are marked Out of Office</li>
		<li>Are inactive or offline (if applicable)</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="5%EF%B8%8F%E2%83%A3FallbackScenario"></a>5️⃣ Fallback Scenario</h3>

<ul>
	<li>If no agents are available:
	<ul>
		<li>Case should remain in queue and Superviser/ Admin can view them in Un assigned Tab under case managmnet section</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ul>

            <br/>
        </td>
